    "name": "Great Falls & Potomac Gorge (Northern Virginia)",
    "region_label": "Great Falls",
    "description": "The Potomac Gorge just upriver of Washington, D.C.: Great Falls Park on the Virginia bank (an NPS site administered under the George Washington Memorial Parkway), the dramatic falls and Mather Gorge, and the River/Difficult Run trails down toward the Beltway. Includes Fairfax County's Riverbend Park and Scott's Run Nature Preserve, with the C&O Canal towpath and Great Falls Tavern visible across the river on the Maryland side. Rocky river-gorge singletrack with real relief above the water.",
    "bbox": [-77.3, 38.9, -77.1, 39.05],
    "bbox_comment": "[west, south, east, north] in decimal degrees (WGS84). Covers the VA-side gorge corridor from Riverbend (N) past Great Falls Park down toward Chain Bridge (S), plus the near MD bank (C&O towpath) across the river.",
